
pfQuest_questcache = {
	["A Scholarly Gamble:60:Speak to Lorekeeper Lydros in Dire Maul and inquire about the specialized recipes they have improved upon.:Ah, just the adventurer I was hoping to see! You won't believe what's happened. Our painstakingly researched recipes for potent elixirs have been discreetly acquired by the Shen'dralar, the ancient Highborne scholars. Even more incredible is that they've allegedly refined it further.\n\nI urge you to journey to Dire Maul and consult Lorekeeper Lydros. This is a unique opportunity to access something even more potent than our original concoctions. Go on, find out what they've done with our research."] = {
		[1] = 10088,
	},
	["Order Must Be Restored:60:Assemble an army and travel to the Eastern Plaguelands. Launch a full assault on Nathanos Blightcaller and any Horde filth that may attempt to protect him.\n\nKeep your wits about you, Daidinn. The Horde will defend the ranger lord with their very lives.:Do you know how many ranger lords exist in this world? How many human ranger lords have ever existed?\n\nNathanos' accomplishments were unprecedented. He was a tactical genius, responsible for Alliance victories spanning a decade of conflict.\n\nAnd now... the champion of the Forsaken.\n\nNo. This cannot be. Order must be restored.\n\nGather an army, Daidinn. Return to the Plagues with your army and destroy the Blightcaller.\n\nI wish you luck, Daidinn. Truly, you will need it for this battle."] = {
		[1] = 6187,
	},
	["The Molten Core:60:Kill 1 Fire Lord, 1 Molten Giant, 1 Ancient Core Hound and 1 Lava Surger, then return to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.:Unknown, perhaps it is time to give you a real test.  Are you ready?\n\nAt the bottom of Blackrock Depths is a passage to the Molten Core.  This is a stronghold of our enemy, held by the most powerful servants of fire on this world.\n\nGo to the Molten Core, Unknown.  Show me you have the strength and the will to defeat what you find there.\n\nAnd if you have allies among your people, then rally them.  Nothing short of an army can hope to enter the Molten Core and live."] = {
		[1] = 6822,
	},
	["Jonespyre's Request:50:Speak with Quintis Jonespyre in Feathermoon Stronghold.:Excuse me, friend...\n\nA colleague of mine would like to speak with you about the research you are doing in conjunction with the Cenarion Circle.  He is a druid by the name of Quintis Jonespyre, and he resides in Feathermoon Stronghold, Feralas.  He would like to confer with you about morrowgrain... and he very much would like for you to keep our discussion from the ears of the Arch Druid.\n\nIf you're interested, speak with him; no doubt, all will be revealed once you do."] = {
		[1] = 3787,
	},
	["Counter Strategy:60:Defeat General Drakkisath.:Bad news, Daidinn! We have received reports that Nefarian’s General of the dragonspawn armies, Drakkisath, is winning the fight against the Dark Iron dwarves and might soon be setting his sights outside of Blackrock. In order to ensure that this cunning strategist isn’t going to have the upper hand against us, we want you to put together a select group of elite adventurers and strike preemptively.\n\nThis mission will require more coordination than before as you will be in command of a larger group. We believe that all your past achievements have forged you into a formidable fighter and that you are capable of seeing this through. \n\nShould you be successful, we can use Drakkisath’s resources to bolster our own capabilities. You will stand to benefit too, of course. Take whatever gear you can find in the Upper Blackrock Spire and become stronger together with the Companions!\n"] = {
		[1] = 10030,
	},
	["Testing Your Mettle:60:Bring Grimando the items he's requested.:Well well, it seems you're eager to prove your worth as a craftsman. Good, good, I love ambition. Let's see what you're made of. I need you to craft specific items using only the finest and rarest materials. This task will push you to be resourceful as well as skilled and dedicated. Don't disappoint me, I have high standards."] = {
		[1] = 10075,
	},
	["Egg Freezing:60:Use the Eggscilloscope Prototype on an egg in the Rookery.:Daidinn, I've been working hard on a new device, the eggscilloscope!  It's designed to project a burst of cold energy at the egg of a black dragon... and freeze it solid!  Can you test it for me?\n\nI heard that high up in Blackrock Spire, the dragons have a rookery where they hatch their eggs.  That's where you'll have to go to test the eggscilloscope, and then let me know how it worked!\n\nAnd don't worry.  Frozen dragon eggs should be harmless.  It's the unfrozen ones you have to worry about!"] = {
		[1] = 4734,
	},
	["Doomrigger's Clasp:60:Bring Doomrigger's Clasp to Mayara Brightwing in the Burning Steppes.:There is a chamber, high in Blackrock Spire, that was once called the Hall of Fortune.  It was where the Dark Iron dwarves kept their relics, trophies and objects of art.\n\nThat was long ago.  It is said the hall has collapsed and is now used for... less savory tasks.  But I believe some old dwarven relics may still be found there.\n\nOne such relic is Doomrigger's clasp, with a surface so encrusted with rare gems that it was said to make weep any dwarf who gazes upon it.\n\nThat clasp, Daidinn, is your goal."] = {
		[1] = 4764,
	},
	["The Molten Core:60:Kill 1 Fire Lord, 1 Molten Giant, 1 Ancient Core Hound and 1 Lava Surger, then return to Duke Hydraxis in Azshara.:Daidinn, perhaps it is time to give you a real test.  Are you ready?\n\nAt the bottom of Blackrock Depths is a passage to the Molten Core.  This is a stronghold of our enemy, held by the most powerful servants of fire on this world.\n\nGo to the Molten Core, Daidinn.  Show me you have the strength and the will to defeat what you find there.\n\nAnd if you have allies among your people, then rally them.  Nothing short of an army can hope to enter the Molten Core and live."] = {
		[1] = 6822,
	},
	["Dungeon Licence : T3D:60:Meet the requirements for obtaining a Tier 3 Dungeon Licence.:When the opportunity arises we must take advantage of it, Daidinn. Tougher enemies usually means better gear and a chance for us to scavenge for useful items in the aftermath of battle. But it does not always come down to fighting. Many in our ranks are not fighters, but crafters, gatherers, artisans, illusionists and so on, of various backgrounds and interests. Their skills and abilities are the engine that keeps our organization moving. \n\nWe value those who know how to forge a sword just as much as those who know how to wield it, and even more so those who know how to do both! Expand your horizons, Daidinn, and pick up a profession or ten. You never know what kind of gadgets you may come up with that could turn the tide of a battle. The basic professions we encourage all our members to learn are First Aid and Cooking. These will allow you to become self-sufficient. Besides, nobody wants to fight on an empty stomach. \n"] = {
		[1] = 10022,
	},
	["The Demon Forge:60:Travel to Blackrock Spire and find Goraluk Anvilcrack. Slay him and then use the Blood Stained Pike upon his corpse. After his soul has been siphoned, the pike will be Soul Stained.\n\nYou must also find the Unforged Rune Covered Breastplate.\n\nReturn both the Soul Stained Pike and the Unforged Rune Covered Breastplate to Lorax in Winterspring.:Lorax makes deals, he does not accept them from insignificant mortals.\n\nA deal I shall make with you, however... take this pike, it is imbued with powerful Fel energies. When you find Goraluk Anvilcrack, slay him and drive this pike through his dying heart. His soul he bartered, his soul I shall have. Return the pike and return the breastplate that the thief stole and I shall teach you what it is that he was to learn."] = {
		[1] = 5127,
	},
	["Fire and Brimstone:60:Defeat Ragnaros, the Firelord.:Ragnaros has been reawakened by Sorcerer-Thane Thaurissan and now threatens to reduce Azeroth to ashes. Prepare yourself, Daidinn, for your first trial is by fire. Head down to the very depths of Molten Core and defeat Ragnaros, the Firelord. \n\nTo say that this isn’t an easy task would be a major understatement. You must be prepared! Gather any help you can muster, either from the ranks of the Companions or anyone else who is foolish enough to join you on this perilous endeavor. Molten Core is one of the hottest places in Blackrock Mountain so make sure to bring plenty of fire resistance equipment and aqual dousers. \n\nShould you succeed, you will not only have saved our world, but this will also elevate you in our ranks. Make haste, Daidinn, for the scorched earth is spreading by the day and soon enough there won't be anything left to save.\n"] = {
		[1] = 10034,
	},
	["The Battle of Darrowshire:60:Place the Relic Bundle at the Darrowshire town square.\n\nPrevent Davil Lightfire's death until the death of Horgus.\n\nPrevent Captain Redpath's death until Redpath the Corrupted appears.\n\nDefeat Redpath the Corrupted.\n\nSpeak with the spirit of Joseph Redpath when he appears at the town square, then speak with Pamela at her home.:Now, Daidinn, you will take part in battle of Darrowshire, and you will save Joseph Redpath.\n\nPlace this relic bundle in the Darrowshire town square, and the spirits of Darrowshire will rise.  Join their battle and assure that these two things come to pass: Davil must survive beyond the death of Horgus, and Redpath must survive to be corrupted, then defeated.\n\nAfter defeating the corrupted Redpath, his spirit will be saved.  Speak with him, then return to his daughter Pamela."] = {
		[1] = 5721,
	},
}
